WEBVTT

00:00:02.130 --> 00:00:05.000
Experiment No. 23
GAN-Q

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:06.500
LAB
Experiment No. 23
GAN-Q

00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:07.960
Experiment No. 23
GAN-Q

00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:08.460
Hey, Ueno!

00:00:08.830 --> 00:00:12.960
They all broke at once! These eyeball things.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:19.380
Love always drives me, and yet…

00:00:25.790 --> 00:00:31.830
The wind against the glass 
creates an image of you

00:00:31.830 --> 00:00:37.290
What "color" will that wind be today?
I want to experience it, completely

00:00:37.290 --> 00:00:40.330
Off in the corners of the classroom

00:00:40.330 --> 00:00:43.540
Through the tiniest of magics

00:00:44.130 --> 00:00:48.330
Another miracle occurs!

00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:49.830
A premonition of love

00:00:49.830 --> 00:00:55.540
My heart shouldn't be so uneasy, 
I don't know what's next

00:00:55.540 --> 00:01:00.460
Aah! What is it that throws 
my heart into turmoil?

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:01.960
This sudden spark

00:01:01.960 --> 00:01:07.630
Love always drives me, and yet…

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:12.330
Someone, someday, deliver 
these feelings to you!

00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:14.880
Aaand, there.

00:01:16.290 --> 00:01:18.790
There's no way all these could break at once!

00:01:19.210 --> 00:01:21.080
Lend me your glasses.

00:01:23.130 --> 00:01:24.460
What is all this?

00:01:24.460 --> 00:01:25.920
Well, lemme tell ya...

00:01:26.290 --> 00:01:33.000
Girls kinda don't like being peeped at and stuff,
so when I found this I was like, "BOOM"!

00:01:34.750 --> 00:01:37.000
That explanation was nowhere near sufficient!

00:01:37.250 --> 00:01:40.540
It would seem that some MALES have come
peeping on the Gymnastics Club during training,

00:01:40.540 --> 00:01:42.960
and the girls are none too pleased about it.

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:45.040
So! That is why I made THIS!

00:01:45.630 --> 00:01:46.750
The GAN-Q!

00:01:47.380 --> 00:01:51.230
Footage from eight separate 
eyeball-shaped drones is

00:01:51.230 --> 00:01:54.350
simultaneously sent to a 
dedicated visor-type monitor,

00:01:54.350 --> 00:01:58.380
allowing for independent and
wide-area search of possible hostiles.

00:01:58.830 --> 00:02:03.080
The design is such that should a club member
wear these, any peeper would be instantly detected!

00:02:03.460 --> 00:02:07.290
I get it. So then, the 
Gymnastic Club's, um...

00:02:07.290 --> 00:02:10.000
I'm the club captain, Unogawa!

00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:10.000
BAM!

00:02:11.250 --> 00:02:12.630
Well? Can you fix them?

00:02:12.630 --> 00:02:14.790
I AM fixing them. Just wait a minute.

00:02:28.880 --> 00:02:30.460
So, how are these, would you say?

00:02:30.460 --> 00:02:31.500
Huh?

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:34.250
Like, how do they work.

00:02:34.670 --> 00:02:37.690
Well, yeah, I guess they work, but 
it's kind of a hassle and stuff

00:02:37.690 --> 00:02:39.990
and I get distracted and all that...

00:02:40.540 --> 00:02:43.710
How come I gotta be the one on lookout duty?

00:02:44.080 --> 00:02:45.500
Because you're the club leader.

00:02:45.830 --> 00:02:48.580
Oh, I know! YOU should be on lookout, Ueno.

00:02:48.580 --> 00:02:50.920
I have nothing to do with 
the Gymnastics Club.

00:02:50.920 --> 00:02:53.330
There ya go, like this doesn't concern you...

00:02:53.330 --> 00:02:57.330
Hey, why don't you give
gymnastics a shot? C'mon, yeah? C'mon.

00:02:57.330 --> 00:02:58.380
Not my problem.

00:02:59.790 --> 00:03:02.420
Hey! What's up with this belly?!

00:03:02.420 --> 00:03:03.500
Stop that.

00:03:03.500 --> 00:03:07.580
It's a bit flabby, wouldn't you say?
You need to exercise more!

00:03:07.580 --> 00:03:09.670
Why not try out for 
gymnastics, huh? Gymnastics!

00:03:07.580 --> 00:03:14.500
Water Storage and Management
for the Aftermath

00:03:09.670 --> 00:03:13.210
The legends passed down to us
say that gymnastics is best for this!

00:03:13.210 --> 00:03:14.500
Oh, be quiet.

00:03:14.500 --> 00:03:16.500
LAB

00:03:18.580 --> 00:03:23.170
So, what does this "Science Club" do?
Like, everyone's just on their own.

00:03:23.170 --> 00:03:26.500
You're all getting flabby
stomachs because you're so lazy!

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:28.750
And then, there's this ass!

00:03:29.330 --> 00:03:30.210
Stop that!

00:03:30.880 --> 00:03:35.920
Take a look at this body of mine, yeah?
It's a miracle of this world, perhaps?

00:03:36.710 --> 00:03:38.630
You're not all that different 
from me, you know.

00:03:38.630 --> 00:03:42.540
Nah, don't compare THIS to 
that flabby body of yours.

00:03:42.540 --> 00:03:45.380
Um... Can I ask something?

00:03:46.250 --> 00:03:47.210
Whatcha want?

00:03:47.210 --> 00:03:48.630
Are you two...

00:03:49.420 --> 00:03:51.250
close like THAT?

00:03:52.080 --> 00:03:53.960
What do you mean, "Like THAT"?

00:03:52.380 --> 00:03:53.920
What do you mean, "Like THAT"?

00:03:54.380 --> 00:03:55.920
Yeah, we're like THAT.

00:03:57.170 --> 00:03:58.920
WHAT DO MEAN, "LIKE THAT"?

00:03:57.330 --> 00:03:59.000
What do you mean, "Like THAT"?

00:03:59.460 --> 00:04:02.830
Um, well, it's hardly my place to say, but...

00:04:03.170 --> 00:04:05.830
There's such a thing as politeness,
even between friends,

00:04:06.080 --> 00:04:10.000
So talking about physical attributes
is... how can I put this?

00:04:10.540 --> 00:04:13.580
They say the skeletal structure
between men and women is different,

00:04:14.080 --> 00:04:16.540
so I feel bad for even making a comparison...

00:04:18.420 --> 00:04:19.960
You ain't made no comparison.

00:04:19.960 --> 00:04:24.330
Um, well, it's about what 
you mentioned earlier...

00:04:30.960 --> 00:04:35.130
Um, I'm sorry. I think maybe
I'm not using the right words.

00:04:35.130 --> 00:04:40.500
Um, the thing is... First of all,
Unogawa-senpai, you're a man, right?

00:04:40.500 --> 00:04:42.210
I'M A WOMAN!

00:04:42.630 --> 00:04:43.460
Huh?

00:04:43.790 --> 00:04:45.670
Why are you so surprised?!

00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:48.330
Well, you've been talking 
like a man, haven't you?

00:04:48.500 --> 00:04:53.500
You got a problem with that?
Your standards of judgment are WAY off!

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:56.540
You can tell by looking, right?!

00:04:59.420 --> 00:05:01.540
Ueno! This fool is just rude!

00:05:01.540 --> 00:05:02.500
Yeah, he's rude.

00:05:04.250 --> 00:05:05.500
Okay, look HERE.

00:05:05.500 --> 00:05:09.880
See? Look here. These are what girls wear.

00:05:09.880 --> 00:05:11.000
Yes, that's true...
See? Look! Check 'em!

00:05:11.000 --> 00:05:12.250
That's not the way to show those!

00:05:15.830 --> 00:05:17.750
Thank you, Ueno!

00:05:18.170 --> 00:05:19.500
Well, see you!

00:05:21.880 --> 00:05:23.920
Hey! You left some of your eyes behind!

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:24.380
SCIENCE

00:05:25.580 --> 00:05:26.710
I swear...

00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:34.290
Hey, dullard! I don't care 
if you didn't mean any harm:

00:05:34.290 --> 00:05:36.080
mistaking a girl for a boy is in no way cool.

00:05:36.080 --> 00:05:37.880
Okay. I'm sorry.

00:05:38.670 --> 00:05:43.670
Unogawa basically says
what she thinks and listens when she wants.

00:05:44.130 --> 00:05:47.750
So I don't think she's too beat up about it.
So, you know... I'm not that upset, either.

00:05:48.630 --> 00:05:49.830
Understood.

00:05:51.380 --> 00:05:53.420
You know, I'm sort of relieved.

00:05:53.880 --> 00:05:54.540
Yeah.

00:06:01.500 --> 00:06:04.540
...Aren't you going to ask 
WHAT he's relieved about?

00:06:07.670 --> 00:06:09.960
Tambo! Tam...bo!

00:06:09.960 --> 00:06:11.380
Yamashita, what's with you?

00:06:17.670 --> 00:06:18.630
LAB

00:06:18.170 --> 00:06:19.420
Yo, Tanaka!

00:06:18.630 --> 00:06:20.500
LAB
Experiment No. 24
Ballet-tan

00:06:19.420 --> 00:06:20.460
Yes, what is it?

00:06:20.500 --> 00:06:23.460
Death by Tofu
Experiment No. 24
Ballet-tan

00:06:20.630 --> 00:06:21.630
Yo, Tanaka!

00:06:22.130 --> 00:06:23.130
Yes, what is it?

00:06:23.710 --> 00:06:28.170
If this MYSTERIOUS gum is desired by many,
by what means would you procure it?

00:06:29.080 --> 00:06:31.880
Well, let's see... We could 
break it up to share with-

00:06:31.880 --> 00:06:33.210
Shut that mouth!

00:06:33.630 --> 00:06:36.380
Material sharing has been 
relegated to the past!

00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:39.750
Now is the age of exchange 
based on EMOTION...

00:06:39.750 --> 00:06:42.210
Through the use of the Ballet-tan!

00:06:43.920 --> 00:06:44.830
The Ballet-tan!

00:06:45.580 --> 00:06:50.420
The encephalic unit measures primary sensory
elements transmitted to the gustatory area,

00:06:51.420 --> 00:06:54.330
and then, upon redirecting the
parsed data to the ring-shaped armlet,

00:06:54.330 --> 00:06:56.750
shares that information via handshake
to whomever wears the same device,

00:06:56.750 --> 00:07:01.000
allowing the recipient to vicariously share
in the taste experience of the primary wearer.

00:06:59.420 --> 00:07:08.000
SWEET!!

00:07:02.540 --> 00:07:07.130
So, basically, shaking hands will directly
transmit how you think things taste and stuff.

00:07:08.000 --> 00:07:08.500
You've pointed a lost alien
family in the right direction.
Collect 10 million yen
and advance 10 spaces.

00:07:08.250 --> 00:07:10.040
That seems like it would be really useful.

00:07:08.500 --> 00:07:13.000
You've pointed a lost alien
family in the right direction.
Collect 10 million yen
and advance 10 spaces.
*FOR ILLUSTRATIVE PURPOSES

00:07:10.040 --> 00:07:13.000
Still, it's not how something actually tastes:
it's your perception of HOW it tastes.

00:07:13.420 --> 00:07:17.250
All right, let's try this thing out!
What flavor is this mysterious gum?

00:07:17.250 --> 00:07:19.750
Think you can grab a paw and figure it out?!

00:07:29.580 --> 00:07:33.790
Oh, sorry. I forgot to put it 
on, which is sort of the point.

00:07:34.170 --> 00:07:37.000
Right now, we were just holding hands.

00:07:40.420 --> 00:07:41.250
Ma'am?

00:07:42.380 --> 00:07:43.880
Do you not want to try it out?

00:07:43.880 --> 00:07:47.290
Whoa-whoa-whoa, well, yeah!

00:07:47.290 --> 00:07:51.400
So, let's get on with it. 
Yamashita, you stay on my right.

00:07:51.400 --> 00:07:54.290
So, starting out with the gum, we'll...

00:08:01.460 --> 00:08:02.960
Y-Yamashita?

00:08:19.170 --> 00:08:20.790
Are you ready?

00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:23.830
Yes, all ready! Hurry up with that gum!

00:08:24.580 --> 00:08:26.130
Okay, here goes.

00:08:29.500 --> 00:08:31.500
Oh! Yes, there we go!

00:08:31.500 --> 00:08:37.080
This flavor is... Well, Yamashita, 
let's say it together.

00:08:37.540 --> 00:08:38.880
One, two... Cantalou-

00:08:38.880 --> 00:08:40.130
I'm not getting anything.

00:08:42.750 --> 00:08:44.460
The flavor hasn't reached me.

00:08:44.960 --> 00:08:46.830
I-I wonder why that is...

00:08:46.830 --> 00:08:49.420
Because that person there 
isn't holding your hand right.

00:08:50.130 --> 00:08:51.210
What, so, here?

00:08:51.210 --> 00:08:52.830
Yes. There.

00:08:53.630 --> 00:08:55.170
Yamashita!

00:08:55.170 --> 00:08:59.000
Ma'am, please pull yourself together.
It's all right to just say it.

00:08:59.000 --> 00:09:02.000
Say, "Interlock your fingers with mine."

00:09:02.250 --> 00:09:05.000
SHOCK!

00:09:05.000 --> 00:09:08.000
HNGRARRGH

00:09:08.420 --> 00:09:11.750
Um, I'm really sorry, but...

00:09:12.420 --> 00:09:15.790
It looks like the signal 
just isn't quite enough.

00:09:16.420 --> 00:09:20.710
It's the WAY the hands are being held...

00:09:21.420 --> 00:09:22.750
The fingers...

00:09:23.540 --> 00:09:26.830
The fingers should be reciprocal, as in...

00:09:27.380 --> 00:09:31.130
Might as that you please 
thrust them into mine?

00:09:31.710 --> 00:09:33.880
Oh, okay. Understood.

00:09:34.710 --> 00:09:36.880
You mean, how couples hold hands, right?

00:09:40.460 --> 00:09:44.000
Um! I'm quite sorry, but...

00:09:44.380 --> 00:09:48.210
On my end, it was meant as
something not quite that serious!

00:09:48.500 --> 00:09:53.330
It's troubling to have this 
thought in such a manner!

00:09:48.750 --> 00:09:51.460
SIGH

00:09:53.830 --> 00:09:56.710
Actually, come to think of it,
I have some errands to run today.

00:09:57.830 --> 00:10:03.540
So, let's call quits here and now! BYE!

00:10:03.960 --> 00:10:06.330
B-bye...

00:10:09.130 --> 00:10:10.290
Tanaka-senpai.

00:10:10.290 --> 00:10:11.250
Huh?

00:10:13.080 --> 00:10:16.630
Ow, ow! Whoa, you're REALLY angry today!
